ESPGeiger's own libraries (EG*). Third party code kept as it came is in vendor/.

EGTcp, EGMqtt and the EGHttp client replaced the patched AsyncTCP, async-mqtt-client
and AsyncHTTPRequest copies in 0.14. Units up for months were losing heap to
connections stuck closing, and on the ESP32 the async callbacks ran on another task,
so every fix needed a lock. One small TCP layer run from loop() on both chips turned
out easier to keep right than patching three libraries.
